GS run expansion: one helper for the per-primitive batch layout shared by both SubmitRun paths (no behaviour change)

`SubmitRun` expands a run primitive into a `GSPrimitiveBatch` in two paths (the per-primitive `Submit` path and the
`GsInventory` path). Both repeated the same vertex-count clamp, copy and zero-filled tail; the tail also has to match
what the `Op::Run` encoder writes. They now call one `fillRunPrimitive`, so the two consumers cannot drift apart.
Same vertices, same tail, +14/-10 lines.

Verified with patch 89 in the same binary: four 63 s ship-deck runs, `anomalies=0`, `levelReady=1`, `run_drops=0`.

